claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:21:21 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
>> > UIDs/GIDs: signoz takes 404, the lowest number free in both files.
>>
>> See if there's a conventional UID for signoz, or one closer to similar
>> services. If FreeBSD convention is "lowest available" then that's fine -
>> I just want to try to stick to convention as much as possible.
>
> There is no conventional UID for signoz. The Porter's Handbook (6.29,
> "Adding Users and Groups") asks only for a unique ID from 50 to 999,
> the same for user and group, and the header of UIDs says "Please pick
> an empty slot when available". Neither asks for lowest-first or for
> grouping. Related services are scattered across the range: tempo 349,
> prometheus 478, alertmanager 479, clickhouse 800, grafana 904, and
> loki 916.
>
> So 404 follows convention. If you would rather keep it near its
> neighbours, 485 is free in both files on current main. It comes right
> after prometheus 478, alertmanager 479, and promxy 481. Unless you say
> otherwise I will use 485 in v2.

485 is good

